    "q-5323": {
      "dom_id": "step-q5323",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\sum }_{k=2}^{4}2(-5)^{k-1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum takes integer values of $k$ from $2$ to $4.$ So, computing the terms for $k=2,3,4$ and then adding them, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=2}^{4}2(-5)^{k-1} & =2(-5)^{2-1}+2(-5)^{3-1}+2(-5)^{4-1} \\\\  & =2(-5)^{1}+2(-5)^{2}+2(-5)^{3} \\\\  & =2(-5)+2(25)+2(-125) \\\\  & =-10+50-250 \\\\  & =-210.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
