    "q-66994": {
      "dom_id": "step-q66994",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Express $S=5+10+15+⋯+145+150$ in sigma notation.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the terms of the corresponding sequence\n\n$$\n5,\\,10,\\,15,\\,…,\\,145,\\,150.\n$$\n\n are multiples of $5,$ and since $150÷5=30,$ there are $30$ terms in total. \n\nTherefore, the $n$th term of the sequence has the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=5n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ ranges from $n=1$ to $n=30.$ Indeed: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =5(1)=5 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =5(2)=10 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =5(3)=15 \\\\  & \\,\\,⋮ \\\\ {a}_{29} & =5(29)=145 \\\\ {a}_{30} & =5(30)=150\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S=5+10+15+⋯+145+150={\\sum }_{n=1}^{30}5n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
